WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.903
-Yet another associate
of former President Trump

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.037
has been arrested.

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:07.006
This time,
it was the former chair

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:08.874
of his inaugural committee,
Tom Barrack,

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:11.277
who is accused of illegally
using his connections

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:14.213
and access to Trump to lobby on
behalf of a foreign government.

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:16.949
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:20.319
♪♪

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.021
There's a lot going on
in the world right now --

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.357
Delta variant, climate disaster,
wealth hoarding,

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.226
tax dodging, tech billionaires
who exploit their workers,

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:30.163
racing to space in cowboy hats
like Data,

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.031
playing sheriff on the holodeck.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.432
Second Data ref in a week.

00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:35.968
Is next generation
our new "MASH"?

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:39.505
But I'd like to start
with perhaps the most trivial

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:42.142
and least consequential
development in the news.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:44.677
Disney unveiling its new
Joe Biden animatronic

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.078
for the Hall of Presidents.

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:47.480
Look at that!

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:52.284
Joe Biden was basically made
to be in the Hall of Presidents.

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.720
You can't tell the difference
between the real Biden

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.256
and the animatronic Biden.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:58.758
In fact, given how much of
a wild card human Biden can be,

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.493
I'm betting his aides
would love

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.861
to have the animatronic
on standby for town halls.

00:01:02.861 --> 00:01:05.832
"Oh, God. Oh, he's telling
the Corn Pops story again.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:08.167
Bring in the robot.
Oh, phew.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.703
Oh, now the robot's telling
the Corn Pops story.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.638
Oh, wait. But, okay,
I can actually follow it.

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:14.040
I can follow
when the robot does it."

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.042
And I have to say
I enjoy the fact

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.444
that Disney made a realistic

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.379
Biden robot with
a presidential demeanor

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.114
and a normal
human facial expression,

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.715
as opposed to
the Trump animatronic,

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.952
which has the expression
of someone who just walked in

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:28.253
on their parents having sex.

00:01:28.253 --> 00:01:30.055
I mean, lookit.

00:01:30.055 --> 00:01:31.591
This looks like
one of the bodies

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:34.293
preserved in ash at Pompeii.

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:37.430
"Vesuvius is never gonna blow.
Yikes!"

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:43.503
Looks like Han Solo
frozen in Carbonite.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:47.873
Also, who signed off
on making Franklin Pierce

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:49.875
look exactly like me?

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:52.779
You gave me one of
the worst presidents.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.113
I grew up in New Hampshire,

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:56.081
so I actually know some stuff
about Franklin Pierce.

00:01:56.081 --> 00:01:57.550
He was also from New Hampshire.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.220
And nothing else.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.054
I remember in fourth grade,

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:04.023
they told us that
New Hampshire news,

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.592
we lost our [bleep]

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.626
And then it was on
to James Buchanan.

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:09.796
Look, maybe one
of the reason --

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.098
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:14.300
Guys, don't laugh
at the Easter eggs.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.369
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:19.205
Maybe one of the reasons

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.540
Trump's animatronic figure
looks so surprised

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.776
is it keeps finding out
more about

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.778
just how corrupt the campaign
and presidency

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.246
of the man he was based on were.

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:29.348
Every day, it seems like
we get new details

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:32.118
about alleged crimes involving
Trump's cabinet officials

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:34.254
or his business associates
or his friends.

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:36.789
Some of them are investigations
we didn't even know about.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.825
It's like a game of Clue
where every answer is correct.

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:41.694
Was it Professor Plum in
the ballroom with the dagger?

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.095
It was.

00:02:43.095 --> 00:02:45.231
How about Miss Scarlet in
the kitchen with the lead pipe?

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.599
Her, too.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.568
Okay, and what about Rudy
in the billiard room

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.136
with the candlestick
to the nuts?

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.071
Yep. Every time.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.639
For example,
we learned this week

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.041
that an inspector general found

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.042
that Trump Commerce Secretary
Wilbur Ross

00:02:57.042 --> 00:02:58.944
lied to Congress
about the census

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:01.447
and presented those findings
to the Trump Justice Department.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:03.416
But Trump's DOJ
declined to prosecute him.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.885
And when Ross heard
he wasn't getting prosecuted,

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.454
I'm guessing he celebrated
by cracking open a beer

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:09.955
and a can of soup.

00:03:09.955 --> 00:03:11.991
I mean, look at him.
That looks like the poster

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.426
for a movie called
"Retirement Frat."

00:03:14.426 --> 00:03:18.698
"Wilbur, did you replace the
oxygen tanks with helium again?"

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.633
-I'll never tell, dude.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:23.036
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.472
That -- That is --

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:30.042
What you just saw
is 100% my fault.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:32.511
And then there's Trump's
former campaign chairman
Paul Manafort.

00:03:32.511 --> 00:03:34.113
A week ago, we found out

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:37.449
that a banker who arranged
millions in loans to Manafort

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:39.785
was found guilty
of trying to use those loans

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:42.822
to secure a job in the Trump
campaign and administration.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:45.324
-It took a federal jury
less than two hours

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:47.326
to reach a guilty verdict
in the case

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:50.829
of former Federal Savings Bank
executive Stephen Calk.

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:53.432
-He was accused of
pushing risky loans through

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:57.036
for former Donald Trump
campaign manager Paul Manafort

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:59.538
in exchange for
a high-level position

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:01.140
in the administration.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:05.477
Calk got Manafort $16 million
worth of loans from the bank,

00:04:05.477 --> 00:04:07.780
despite concerns
from board members

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.582
over their high levels
of risk.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.451
Manafort then recommended Calk

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:14.687
for an open undersecretary
of the Army position.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:17.323
-Look, I'm sure this sort of
[bleep] happens all the time
in D.C.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.925
and more people
should be prosecuted for it,

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:21.660
but, my God, Trump and his
cronies were so brazen about it.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:24.697
The Trump operation was such
a toxic criminal enterprise

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:27.199
that even people who are
just tangentially related to him

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:28.768
are getting thrown in jail now.

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:30.036
At this point,
I wouldn't be surprised

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.704
if they get his Disney robot

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.806
for using a shell company
to dodge taxes.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:38.043
Don't look surprised.
You know what you did.

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:40.646
Calk apparently got a job
on the Trump campaign

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:41.981
by loaning Manafort millions

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.649
despite his checkered
financial past.

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:46.485
And when Trump won, he actually
wrote down a list of jobs

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:48.688
he would want
in a Trump administration.

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:52.725
-Stephen Calk was convicted
for giving Paul Manafort

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:54.493
$16 million

00:04:54.493 --> 00:04:58.163
in questionable bank loans
in 2016 and 2017.

00:04:58.163 --> 00:05:01.434
After Calk's first multimillion
dollar loan to Manafort,

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.602
Manafort put him
on the Trump campaign's

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:05.137
Economic Advisory Council.

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:06.672
Prosecutors said Stephen Calk

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:09.041
repeatedly ignored
financial red flags

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:10.476
in Manafort's loan applications

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:13.178
because he desperately wanted
to be secretary of the Army

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:15.248
and that's how we could get it.

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:17.049
He listed, in ranked order,

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:20.152
his favored, quote,
"prospective roles" --

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:23.055
prospective roles
in the new administration.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:25.223
His number-one choice
was secretary of the Army.

00:05:25.223 --> 00:05:28.694
If not that, he'd take,
you know, secretary of commerce,

00:05:28.694 --> 00:05:30.763
deputy secretary
of the Treasury,

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.532
18 preferred ambassadorships,

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:35.668
everything from the U.K.
to the Vatican to Singapore.

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:38.070
-I guess if you're the kind
of guy who ignores red flags,

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.306
you're also the kind of guy
who writes down a list

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:43.142
of the quos you would like
in return for your quids.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.078
"Yeah, send a copy of this
to Manafort,

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:46.879
Trump, and, uh, uh, the FBI?

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:48.014
Is that dumb?"

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.348
Also, total aside here,

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:50.649
but if you're a corrupt banker

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:52.551
paying for a job
in the administration,

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:54.353
why would you want
secretary of the Army

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:56.155
over ambassador
to the Vatican?

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:58.991
I mean, the secretary of
the Army has actual stuff to do.

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.892
I'm pretty sure
the ambassador to the Vatican

00:06:00.892 --> 00:06:03.296
just gets to hang out in Rome,
drinking Aperol spritzes,

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:05.898
and dodging Vespas
on cobblestone streets.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:08.467
Every now and then, you run
into the Pope, and he says,

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:11.904
"I'ma from Argentina.
I don't-a talk-a like this."

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:14.540
Of course, Calk wasn't
the only Trump goon

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.041
to write down
incriminating material.

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:17.943
When prosecutors indicted
Trump Organization

00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:19.579
CFO Allen Weisselberg

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:21.513
for alleged tax fraud
earlier this month,

00:06:21.513 --> 00:06:24.182
it turned out they kept
internal spreadsheets

00:06:24.182 --> 00:06:25.317
detailing the scheme.

00:06:25.317 --> 00:06:26.952
For example,
according to the indictment,

00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:29.321
Weisselberg caused
the Trump Corporation

00:06:29.321 --> 00:06:30.589
to issue corporate checks

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:32.624
made payable to
a Trump Organization employee

00:06:32.624 --> 00:06:35.594
who cashed the checks
and received cash.

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:36.995
The cash was given
to Weisselberg

00:06:36.995 --> 00:06:38.364
for his personal use.

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:40.165
The Trump Corporation
booked this cash

00:06:40.165 --> 00:06:41.434
as holiday entertainment

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.202
but maintained
internal spreadsheets

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.470
showing the cash to be part

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.405
of Weisselberg's
employee compensation.

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:48.608
The dead giveaway there is
that Trump would never pay

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:50.275
for holiday entertainment
on Christmas.

00:06:50.275 --> 00:06:52.378
He would sit there
with Eric and Don Jr.

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:53.979
and watch the "Grinch" on TV.

00:06:53.979 --> 00:06:56.281
"Why can't you idiots
be more like this guy?"

00:06:56.281 --> 00:06:58.016
Then yesterday, we got news
about the arrest

00:06:58.016 --> 00:07:01.120
of yet another longtime
Trump associate Tom Barrack,

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.955
who was an adviser
to Trump's campaign

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:04.356
and the chair
of his inaugural committee,

00:07:04.356 --> 00:07:06.792
which incidentally
is also under investigation

00:07:06.792 --> 00:07:08.961
unrelated
to these new charges.

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.129
-Tom Barrack, the chairman

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:12.465
of Trump's 2017
inaugural committee,

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:15.034
has been arrested
on a host of charges,

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:18.204
including illegally lobbying
for the United Arab Emirates,

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:20.806
obstructing justice,
and making false statements

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:22.107
to federal agents.

00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:23.408
"The Washington Post" reports,

00:07:23.408 --> 00:07:25.511
"Federal prosecutors say
Barrack capitalized

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:28.414
on his friendship with
and access to Trump

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:30.883
and other high-ranking
government officials

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:33.285
and his relationship
with U.S. journalists

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:35.888
to advance the policy goals
of a foreign government

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:38.457
without disclosing
their true alliances."

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:40.760
-So one of Trump's closest
confidants and advisers

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:43.295
was secretly using his access
and connection to Trump

00:07:43.295 --> 00:07:45.764
to lobby the campaign
and the administration

00:07:45.764 --> 00:07:47.833
as an unregistered agent
of a foreign government.

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:49.535
That means various
Trump associates

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:52.571
were either lobbying for
or connected to Ukraine,

00:07:52.571 --> 00:07:56.008
Russia, Turkey, Qatar
and the UAE, among others.

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:58.977
That place was like the Epcot
world showcase of corruption.

00:07:58.977 --> 00:08:01.079
This was supposed to be
the America First campaign,

00:08:01.079 --> 00:08:02.481
the new working-class GOP.

00:08:02.481 --> 00:08:04.917
Instead, it was all a bunch
of millionaire lobbyists,

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:07.353
bankers, consultants,
and private equity titans

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:08.888
working for foreign countries.

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:10.389
The so-called America First
campaign

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:12.057
was a bigger scam
than Subway tuna.

00:08:12.057 --> 00:08:14.193
I'm not saying it's not tuna.
All I know is, last week,

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:16.028
I found a wishbone
in my foot-long

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:18.130
and then I pulled it apart
and wished for real tuna.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.299
Now, we already knew
part of this story,

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:22.435
thanks to an investigation
by the House Oversight Committee

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:24.837
during the Trump presidency,
which found that Barrack

00:08:24.837 --> 00:08:28.874
had submitted drafts of a 2016
America First energy speech

00:08:28.874 --> 00:08:30.642
to the UAE for edits.

00:08:30.642 --> 00:08:33.879
He took a speech with
"America First" in the title

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:36.315
and submitted it to a foreign
government for approval.

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:37.950
That's like finding out the cop

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.586
who did the Dare presentation
at your high school

00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:44.356
snorted some fat rails off a
cafeteria tray to get hyped up.

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:46.792
"Whoo! Who's ready to learn
about how bad drugs are?

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:49.795
Wait. Uh, sorry. My friend Pablo
Escobar did a rewrite on that.

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:53.132
Who's ready to find out
how bad drugs aren't?"

00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:55.500
And according to the indictment
released yesterday, Barrack,

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:56.868
a long-time Trump friend,

00:08:56.868 --> 00:08:59.338
used that friendship
to get language inserted

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:02.574
into the then candidate's
energy speech in 2016

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:05.244
about the importance
of working with our Gulf allies

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:07.078
at the behest
of Emirati officials.

00:09:07.078 --> 00:09:09.915
So, thanks to Barrack,
the UAE basically hired Trump

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:11.416
to do a cameo for them.

00:09:11.416 --> 00:09:13.085
"UAE, it's Donald Trump,

00:09:13.085 --> 00:09:15.888
and I hear you have
a birthday coming up."

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:17.456
But Barrack succeeded,
as you can see

00:09:17.456 --> 00:09:19.592
from this clip
of the speech in 2016,

00:09:19.592 --> 00:09:22.394
which was supposed to be about
American energy independence

00:09:22.394 --> 00:09:24.630
and the so-called America First
energy policy.

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:27.299
Weirdly, there was a line
out of nowhere

00:09:27.299 --> 00:09:29.201
where Trump seemed
to backtrack and say,

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:33.372
"Actually, we'll keep buying oil
from Gulf states like the UAE."

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:36.208
-We will become and stay
totally independent

00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:40.012
of any need to import energy
from the OPEC cartel

00:09:40.012 --> 00:09:42.781
or any nations hostile
to our interests --

00:09:42.781 --> 00:09:45.117
anybody hostile
to our interests.

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:47.853
Believe me,
we don't deal with them.

00:09:47.853 --> 00:09:50.889
We'll handle them just fine.
Just fine.

00:09:50.889 --> 00:09:54.426
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:54.426 --> 00:09:56.562
And, by the way, there are
plenty of them out there

00:09:56.562 --> 00:09:59.197
that are hostile
to our interests.

00:09:59.197 --> 00:10:02.902
At the same time,
we'll work with our Gulf allies

00:10:02.902 --> 00:10:06.204
to develop a positive
energy relationship

00:10:06.204 --> 00:10:09.208
as part of our
anti-terrorism strategy.

00:10:09.208 --> 00:10:11.209
-He makes it so easy
for prosecutors.

00:10:11.209 --> 00:10:14.246
You can literally see the moment
where he riffs off the cuff

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:16.214
and then goes back to the line
Barrack wrote for him.

00:10:16.214 --> 00:10:18.584
He totally contradicts himself.
"Those Gulf states,

00:10:18.584 --> 00:10:19.885
they hate us, don't they, folks?

00:10:19.885 --> 00:10:23.189
Mark my words, we will never
work with them, ever.

00:10:23.189 --> 00:10:25.791
Those Gulf states
can kiss my ass.

00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:28.660
At the same time, we will
work with our Gulf allies

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:31.163
because they love us
and we love them.

00:10:31.163 --> 00:10:34.900
And remember, they do
have a birthday Coming up."

